                <pb facs="0358" n="258" sameAs="frus:frus1920v03/pg258"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">125.61383 J 41/64: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Mexico</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Summerlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-06-29T18:00:00-06:36"><hi rendition="#italic">June 29, 1920—6
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:11 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>311. Local press to-day states that, in a renewed investigation of the Jenkins
                    case in Puebla, a number of peon witnesses testified that their original
                    testimony, damaging to Jenkins, was false and was extorted under torture and
                    threats of death, and Cordova, now a general in the Army, testified that he
                    alone is responsible for the abduction.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Summerlin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
